WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.960
readWords cooperatively initialises shared words, then all threads reach a barrier.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.860
Each lane reads words[lane * stride].

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.875
The returned integers identify word addresses.

00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:17.880
The host calculates service rounds for the stated bank model; the console is not a hardware timer.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.305
Initialise shared words.

00:00:21.305 --> 00:00:23.865
Complete the block barrier before reads.

00:00:23.865 --> 00:00:25.115
Select words.

00:00:25.115 --> 00:00:27.480
Each lane forms lane × stride.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.815
Group by bank.

00:00:28.815 --> 00:00:32.095
Distinguish broadcasts from different-word conflicts.

00:00:33.595 --> 00:00:38.460
Shared memory is organised into banks that can serve requests in parallel.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.740
In this model, word index modulo 32 selects a bank.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:48.540
Repeated requests for one word can broadcast; different words in one bank need separate rounds.
